      "content": "It means acknowledging that the fight itself is what's draining you, the constant effort to force the old energy back when it's gone. Rebuilding isn't always about putting the pieces back; sometimes it's about letting the wreckage rest. That quiet peace is the permission to stop performing, to just *be* in the stillness without the pressure to be something else. It's a gentle surrender to the fact that the foundation was always just a temporary structure.",
